By default, you generally don't need to enable SharePoint Search manually.
In SharePoint Online, most site, list, library, page, and column content is crawled and added to the search index by default. 
Enable content on a site to be searchable

So normally:
    Upload/Create content
     → SharePoint indexes it
     → User searches
     → Results appear according to permissions

1)When would you configure Search?
You may configure it when you want to:
      Exclude a Site from search
      Exclude a List/Library from search
      Re-index a Site/List/Library
      Configure advanced Search Schema
      Work with Crawled Properties / Managed Properties
      Customize how specific metadata is searchable

SharePoint provides those search settings, but you don't configure them for normal everyday searching.
Manage the search schema in SharePoint
